  "title": "CHAPTER 1: HISTORY OF GOA",
  "order": 1,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "r1713zf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Ancient History of Goa"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient Goa's early medieval era saw rule by the Maurya, Satavahana, Bhojas, and the Kadamba Dynasty (960–1312 CE).",
        "During the medieval period, control over Goa transitioned between the Vijayanagara Empire, Bahamani Sultanate, and the Portuguese.",
        "Portuguese rule officially began with the conquest of Goa in 1510 and included the Goa Inquisition from 1560 to 1812.",
        "The freedom movement culminated in the liberation of Goa via Operation Vijay on December 18–19, 1961."
      ],
      "id": "foflgdz"
    },
